  "answer_text": "Here are some of the **best free online auto repair estimate tools** available:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 1. [RepairPal Estimator](https://repairpal.com/estimator)\nRepairPal has been the #1 automotive industry estimator since 2008, developed by ASE-certified mechanics, and is trusted by millions of consumers and over 3,800 RepairPal Certified locations. The estimator combines automotive industry standard data for parts pricing and labor times with a proprietary labor rate model to deliver fair price ranges for common repairs and services. If the repair cost exceeds the estimate range, they can intervene to work with the shop on your behalf or refund the difference \u2014 and the shop agrees to honor the RepairPal Price Guarantee for 30 days after the repair is performed.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 2. [Kelley Blue Book (KBB) Auto Repair Estimator](https://www.kbb.com/auto-repair/)\nKBB offers a free car repair estimator to find out what you should expect to pay for common auto repairs and maintenance. Estimating repair costs using their tool is considered the best and easiest way to know how much you can expect to pay, based on what others have paid.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 3. [YourMechanic](https://www.yourmechanic.com/estimates/)\nYourMechanic provides free instant auto repair and maintenance estimates with a full price breakdown including parts and labor. They have provided over 600,000 car repair estimates since 2012. You can choose from 600+ repair, maintenance, and diagnostic services, all backed by a 12-month, 12,000-mile warranty. Their mechanics are fully mobile with no brick-and-mortar shop to maintain, which means very low overhead costs \u2014 and those savings are passed on to you.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 4. [NAPA Auto Care Repair Estimator](https://www.napaonline.com/en/auto-care/car-repair-estimator)\nNAPA's tool lets you find out the cost of a repair to your exact make and model before you schedule an appointment \u2014 it's a quick and easy way to get price estimates for the most common car repairs and routine maintenance services.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 5. [Maaco Online Estimator](https://www.maaco.com/online-estimator/) *(Body & Paint)*\nMaaco offers a free online estimate specifically for auto body repair, painting, and collision repair services.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 6. [Instant Estimator](https://www.instantestimator.com/) *(Auto Body)*\nInstant Estimator is one of the first auto body damage estimating tools and also connects you to authorized auto body repair facilities in your area. Best of all \u2014 it's completely free!\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Tips for Using Online Repair Estimates:\n- **Get multiple quotes** \u2014 compare at least 2\u20133 shops before committing.\n- Once you know the estimated range of a typical repair using a car repair tool, you equip yourself with knowledge of the costs \u2014 while fixed costs like the price for the car part may not be negotiable, dealerships and car repair shops will sometimes offer a break.\n- If it's a common repair or maintenance item, like an oil change, new brakes, or a tune-up, you can often find a promotion or coupon.\n- The best way to keep your car repair costs low is to keep up with regular maintenance on your vehicle.",
